ny lines.\n\n*Covering property.*  \nFor each \\(t\\in T\\) the point \\((t,1)\\) loses the vertical line \\(x=t\\) but belongs to \\(S_{t}\\). No other point of \\(\\mathcal P_{n}\\) is affected, because the vertical lines \\(x=t\\) intersect \\(\\mathcal P_{n}\\) only at points with second coordinate \\(b\\ge 1\\), all of which are still covered by the horizontal line \\(y=1\\) or by other vertical lines. Hence every \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal P_{n}\\) lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L_{T}\\).\n\nTherefore for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-1\\) we have constructed a family of \\(n\\) distinct lines containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5. The case \\(k=n\\)\n\nStart from \\(\\mathcal L_{0}\\) and replace **all** vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n-1\\) by the sunny lines \\(S_{1},\\dots ,S_{n-1}\\) as above.  \nAt this stage the point \\((n,1)\\) is still covered only by the horizontal line \\(y=1\\), which is non‑sunny. Replace this horizontal line by the sunny line  \n\n\\[\nS_{n}:\\; y = x-(n-1) .\n\\]\n\nIndeed, substituting \\(x=n\\) gives \\(y=n-(n-1)=1\\), so \\((n,1)\\in S_{n}\\).  \n\\(S_{n}\\) has slope \\(1\\), hence it is sunny.  \n\nThe resulting family  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal L_{n}= \\{S_{1},S_{2},\\dots ,S_{n-1},S_{n}\\}\n\\]\n\ncontains \\(n\\) distinct sunny lines and still covers every point of \\(\\mathcal P_{n}\\) (the argument is identical to the one in Section 4). Thus a configuration with \\(k=n\\) sunny lines exists.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6. Conclusion  \n\nWe have exhibited, for each \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\), an explicit set of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering requirement and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines. Since a configuration cannot have more than \\(n\\) sunny lines, the set of admissible \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\nThis completes the solution.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
